Subject: [PATCH] turn: the forced first site must always land under the avatar

A player who already controls a site somewhere else can never establish a domain
under their own avatar.

`afterDrawStep`'s forced establishment plays the site at the avatar's own square but
calls `playSite` WITHOUT `force`, so the placement goes through `legalSiteSquares`.
That helper switches rule as soon as you control a site:

    baseSiteSquares()  // casting.ts
      no sites yet -> the squares closest to your avatar   (your own square qualifies)
      any site     -> only squares bordering a site you control

So once a player owns one site that does not touch their avatar, their avatar's own
square stops being offered, `playSite` returns "You cannot play a site there", and
`turn:firstSite` logs "First site could not be placed" and leaves `established`
false. The avatar then has no domain for the rest of the game.

This is reachable in normal play, and not rare: Imperial Road's Genesis ("Target
opponent, then you, may play a site adjacent to this one") hands the OPPONENT a site
placed with `force: true` beside the road. If that square does not border their
avatar, their own first-site establishment is dead before their first turn starts.

Reproduced on a fresh game: before owning any site the avatar's square is the only
legal square; after being given a site three rows away it is not offered at all.

The fix is what `force` is documented for — "a card dictates WHERE ... The caller is
responsible for validating the square". Here the ENGINE dictates the square: it is
the avatar's own, by rule ("Play your first site — placed under your avatar"), so the
adjacency rule should not be consulted. Occupancy is still checked inside playSite.

Both forced paths are corrected: the Pathfinder-style auto-establish and the ordinary
`turn:firstSite` continuation.

--- a/packages/shared/src/engine/turn.ts
+++ b/packages/shared/src/engine/turn.ts
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@
       p.hand.push(cardId) // playSite plays from hand
       const tap = canTap(state, avatar)
       if (tap) tapUnit(state, avatar) // uses the avatar's own ability
-      const err = playSite(state, player, cardId, avatar.x, avatar.y) // fires Genesis
+      const err = playSite(state, player, cardId, avatar.x, avatar.y, { force: true }) // fires Genesis
       if (err) {
         // revert on the (near-impossible) illegal placement
         const i = p.hand.indexOf(cardId)
@@ -323,7 +323,7 @@
     // Special avatars that play sites through their own ability pay their own cost.
     const tap = !getScript(avatar.name)?.noStandardSiteAction && canTap(state, avatar)
     if (tap) tapUnit(state, avatar)
-    const err = playSite(state, ctx.player, cardId, avatar.x, avatar.y) // fires the site's Genesis
+    const err = playSite(state, ctx.player, cardId, avatar.x, avatar.y, { force: true }) // fires the site's Genesis
     if (err) {
       if (tap) avatar.tapped = false // refund the tap on an illegal placement
       pushLog(state, ctx.player, `First site could not be placed: ${err}`)
